# Credentials for the credentialed pipeline stages. Copy to .env and fill in.
# .env is gitignored; never commit real credentials.
#
# Create an API Client in the Merchant Center under Settings → Developer
# settings. Scopes needed:
#
#   preflight            view_project_settings
#   preflight --apply    manage_project_settings
#   load                 manage_products, manage_import_containers
#   load (standalone)    ...plus manage_standalone_prices
#   load (channels)      ...covered by manage_products
#   load (customer grps) ...plus view_customer_groups, manage_customer_groups
#   verify               view_products (+ view_standalone_prices for standalone)
#
# manage_products also grants the Import Requests for categories, product
# types, products, product variants and embedded prices, and covers reading and
# creating channels. It does NOT grant Standalone Prices — that needs
# manage_standalone_prices, so a client built for an embedded-price load fails
# on the standalone stage alone, with a 403 — and it does not grant customer
# groups either. `load` creates channels and customer groups that the project
# is missing, because the Import API has no resource for either, so a feed
# declaring a customerGroup needs both customer-group scopes.
#
# NOTE ON PRECEDENCE: exported environment variables win over this file, with
# two exceptions, both about which project a run targets.
#
#   1. If both name a CTP_PROJECT_KEY and the two disagree, the run is refused
#      rather than resolved. Pointing --env at a second project's file while
#      the first project is still exported in your shell is the one mistake
#      worth making impossible.
#
#   2. If this file does NOT exist and the environment names a project, the run
#      is also refused. A directory with no credentials of its own is where a
#      run silently borrows whatever project you happened to export — a dogfood
#      run did exactly that and targeted a project nobody chose. Set
#      CTP_AMBIENT_OK=1 to declare an ambient environment deliberate, which is
#      what CI and containers should do.

CTP_PROJECT_KEY=
CTP_CLIENT_ID=
CTP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# One of: us-central1.gcp, us-east-2.aws, europe-west1.gcp, eu-central-1.aws,
# australia-southeast1.gcp. This derives all three hosts.
CTP_REGION=europe-west1.gcp

# Override the hosts individually instead of using CTP_REGION if you need to.
# Note that the Import API is on a different host from the HTTP API.
# CTP_AUTH_URL=https://auth.europe-west1.gcp.commercetools.com
# CTP_API_URL=https://api.europe-west1.gcp.commercetools.com
# CTP_IMPORT_URL=https://import.europe-west1.gcp.commercetools.com

# Optional. Omitting it grants the token every scope the API Client has, which
# is normally what you want.
# CTP_SCOPES=
